*
a298 65
*   Write out a wcsprm struct as FITS header cards; wcshdo()
*   --------------------------------------------------------
*   wcshdo() translates a wcsprm struct into FITS header cards.  If the colnum
*   member of the struct is non-zero then binary table image array cards will
*   be produced.  Otherwise, if the colax[] member of the struct is set non-
*   zero then pixel list cards will be produced.  Otherwise, primary image or
*   image extension header cards will be produced.
*
*   If the struct was originally constructed from a header, e.g. by wcspih,
*   the output cards will almost certainly differ in a number of respects:
*
*     1) The output header only contains WCS-related cards.  In particular, it
*        does not contain syntactically-required cards such as SIMPLE, NAXIS,
*        BITPIX, or END.
*
*     2) Deprecated (e.g. CROTAn) or non-standard usage will be translated to
*        standard (this is partially dependent on whether wcsfix() was
*        applied).
*
*     3) Quantities will be converted to the units used internally, basically
*        SI with the addition of degrees.
*
*     4) Floating-point quantities may be given to a different decimal
*        precision.
*
*     5) Elements of the PCi_j matrix will be written if and only if they
*        differ from the unit matrix.  Thus, if the matrix is unity then no
*        elements will be written.
*
*     6) Additional keywords such as WCSAXES, CUNITia, LONPOLEa and LATPOLEa
*        may appear.
*
*     7) The original inline comments will be lost, although wcshdo() does try
*        to write meaningful comments.
*
*     8) Card order may be changed.
*
*   Cards can be translated between the image array, binary table, and pixel
*   lists forms by manipulating the colnum or colax[] members of the wcsprm
*   struct.
*
*   Given and returned:
*      wcs      struct wcsprm*
*                        Pointer to a wcsprm struct containing coordinate
*                        transformation parameters.  Will be initialized if
*                        necessary.
*
*   Returned:
*      ncards   int*     Number of FITS header cards returned in the 'header'
*                        array.
*      header   char**   Pointer to an array of char holding the header cards.
*                        Storage for the array is allocated by wcshdo() in
*                        blocks of 2880 bytes (32 x 80-character cards) and
*                        must be free'd by the user to avoid memory leaks.
*
*                        Each card is 80 characters long and is *NOT* null-
*                        terminated, so the first card starts at (*header)[0],
*                        the second at (*header)[80], etc.
*
*   Function return value:
*               int      Status return value:
*                           0: Success.
*                           1: Null wcsprm pointer passed.
*
*
a581 1
int wcshdo(struct wcsprm *, int *, char **);
